Issue #378 revision 2 review — DONE

**Fix status:** The mirror-error state **LANDED** at D2 (109) and L4 (203). The Keep recordings eligibility rule **LANDED** at D9 (135). The clean Release default, hidden-route, and History display tests **LANDED** at §11 (239–241). Retained-log disclosure **PARTLY LANDED** at D3 (111) and D5 (127), but D7 (131), the copy note (208), blast radius (261), and Q2 (272) still imply the sentence appears only while On or that logs age out while Off.

**BLOCKING — Off is not true at confirmation.** Concrete interleaving: a writer holds its log lock, sees the flag present, and starts a batch. Main deletes the flag without taking that lock, rereads absence, and shows Off. The writer finishes writing words afterward. A `LocalLog.words` call can likewise pass its flag check just before deletion, then build a string and enqueue after it. The writer’s later check may prevent persistence, but D3’s “no enqueue, no content string built” does not hold at that boundary. The §11 blocked-writer test can pass without exercising a batch already past its check.

**Replace D2’s Off sentence with this verbatim prose:** “To settle Detailed log Off, main acquires the five per-process log locks in fixed order, using the in-process mutex for its own lock. It removes and verifies the flag while holding them, then releases them and shows Off. Each writer checks the flag under its lock immediately before evaluating queued word lambdas or writing a batch, and discards the batch if absent. If any lock cannot be obtained, the page remains Pending or shows an error; it never shows Off.” **Add to §11:** “Pause a writer after its flag check but before its first batch write, request Off, and assert the page cannot confirm Off until that batch completes; after confirmation no further bytes or word strings are produced.”

The crash hook’s Off check and `:audio`’s Keep recordings check have the same read-before-delete window. D9’s later main-side Off check discards a pending link, so I found no additional permanent archive from that window; its stated in-progress-take caveat matters. A crash hook must not bypass the writer’s under-lock Off check when flushing. **Add to D4:** “Crash flush uses the same under-lock flag check as an ordinary batch and cannot write queued content after Off confirms.”

**NON-BLOCKING — per-call `stat` is a hot-path risk.** Logging calls occur on capture and insertion paths, including [AudioCaptureService.kt:598](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/audio/AudioCaptureService.kt:598) and [AccessibilityInsertionRunner.kt:275](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/paste/AccessibilityInsertionRunner.kt:275). Android advises against synchronous storage work on responsive threads. [Android ANR guidance](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/views/vitals/anr-views). The S26 latency result is **NOT VERIFIED**. A cheaper equally strict *file-write* design is a process-local atomic hint plus lazy queue entries, with the writer’s under-lock flag check; it gives up the internal “no enqueue” property. **Add to chunk 1:** “Measure Off-state `File.exists` cost on capture and insertion threads. If it harms the accepted latency, use lazy queue entries and writer-only file gating; no dictated string is evaluated or persisted while Off.”

**NON-BLOCKING — stale copy and telemetry proof.** **Replace D7/Q2’s “ages out” claim with:** “While Detailed log is Off, existing files remain unchanged until later logging overwrites them or the app is uninstalled.” Update lines 208 and 261 to say the Privacy sentence also appears while retained files exist. D5’s assertion that an attempted switch-state telemetry event “would be dropped” is unsupported: [PayloadSanitizer.kt:51](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/telemetry/PayloadSanitizer.kt:51) already allows generic `setting`, `from`, and `to` keys. The event builder is **UNCHECKED**. **Replace that assertion with:** “Toggle handlers deliberately emit no settings-changed telemetry event; test that neither switch name nor value reaches PostHog or Sentry.”

Axes searched: five prior fixes **four landed, disclosure partial**; call versus delete **found race**; batch versus delete **found race**; crash flush **found inherited risk**; Keep close versus Off **bounded by D9’s discard rule**; hot-path `stat` **NOT VERIFIED**; retained-file copy and telemetry allowlist **found stale claims**.

